# ==============================================================================
# Line endings are the REPOSITORY's business, not the clone's.
# ==============================================================================
#
# A clone must not depend on the CLONER's `core.autocrlf` to reproduce the
# tree.  `_verify/_bitexact_mutation_1640.py` matches LITERAL newlines in
# `examples/bitexact/main.mbt`; in a CRLF working tree two of its four
# mutations matched nothing, the battery SKIPPED them, and it exited 1 --
# while the README published "all four mutations killed".  The release
# machine happened to carry a local `core.autocrlf=false`, which is not
# part of the tracked tree, so only the machine that cut the release ever
# saw the claim hold.  A published claim has to hold for the clone a
# reader makes.
#
# Only the SOURCE types are pinned.  The captured artefacts under
# `_verify/` and `_probe/` are BYTE RECORDS of past runs -- golden JSONs,
# raw logs, captured stdout -- and they are committed exactly as they were
# written, CR and all.  Normalising them would rewrite the very evidence
# they are, so they are marked `-text` and are never converted in either
# direction.  `CHANGELOG.md` is in the same category: it is spliced at
# byte level and its CR count is asserted, so it keeps its bytes exactly.
#
# In .gitattributes the LAST matching pattern wins for each attribute, so
# the `-text` rules below deliberately come after the general ones.
# ==============================================================================

*.mbt    text eol=lf
*.mod    text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.toml   text eol=lf
*.ps1    text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
LICENSE  text eol=lf

# --- the byte records: committed exactly as written, never converted --------
CHANGELOG.md                    -text
_prove_pilot2_error.txt         -text
validate_cluster_iv_with_python.py -text
_verify/*.txt                   -text
_verify/*.json                  -text
_verify/*.py                    -text
_probe/*                        -text
